      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "LAC DU FLAMBEAU BAND OF ) LAKE SUPERIOR CHIPPEWA INDIANS, ) ET AL., ) Petitioners, ) v. ) No. 22-227 BRIAN W. COUGHLIN, ) Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16c1f18c99c2c0b3a88a0bf1216fa02155038bf827c4c52533436d86e0f9e5c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16c1f18c99c2-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-22-227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16c1f18c99c2c0b3a88a0bf1216fa02155038bf827c4c52533436d86e0f9e5c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16c1f18c99c2-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: The -- so, in your thinking and argument, Congress would actually have to say \"tribe\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2022-22-227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16c1f18c99c2c0b3a88a0bf1216fa02155038bf827c4c52533436d86e0f9e5c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16c1f18c99c2-0000-0004",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "even after he -- he filed the bankruptcy petition and notified Lendgreen that he had done so, they continued to contact him, and he attempted to commit suicide, and even when he was in the hospital after this unsuccessful attempt, they were calling him at the hospital to collect this loan?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-22-227",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "16c1f18c99c2c0b3a88a0bf1216fa02155038bf827c4c52533436d86e0f9e5c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16c1f18c99c2-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Tell me why Congress would want to leave that unclear."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. SHAH",
      "case_id": "2022-22-227",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "16c1f18c99c2c0b3a88a0bf1216fa02155038bf827c4c52533436d86e0f9e5c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16c1f18c99c2-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SHAH: Well, Your Honor, if it had wanted to clearly include Indian tribes, which, of course, it had to do under this Court's longstanding jurisprudence and reiterated just"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-22-227",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "16c1f18c99c2c0b3a88a0bf1216fa02155038bf827c4c52533436d86e0f9e5c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16c1f18c99c2-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Mr. Shah, I think the gist of some of the questions is, while prevailing here would advantage the tribe, obviously, in terms of monetary claims against it, that it would also mean that you'd lose certain benefits for tribes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-22-227",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "16c1f18c99c2c0b3a88a0bf1216fa02155038bf827c4c52533436d86e0f9e5c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16c1f18c99c2-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Okay. So what if they painstakingly enumerated and let's say said, you know, no sovereign immunity for Indian tribes, the United States, or any other domestic or foreign government."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-22-227",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "16c1f18c99c2c0b3a88a0bf1216fa02155038bf827c4c52533436d86e0f9e5c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16c1f18c99c2-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Petitioner said that the -- there's been a change in the treatment of tribes under the new Bankruptcy Code. Do you agree with Petitioner, or do you -- and if not, could you elaborate on your differences?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court Transcript",
      "case_id": "2022-22-227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16c1f18c99c2c0b3a88a0bf1216fa02155038bf827c4c52533436d86e0f9e5c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16c1f18c99c2-0002-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It lists all these different kinds of governments, governments that really never show up in our abrogation cases. And -- and -- and it doesn't list Indians. It doesn't list tribes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2022-22-227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16c1f18c99c2c0b3a88a0bf1216fa02155038bf827c4c52533436d86e0f9e5c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16c1f18c99c2-0002-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Bankruptcy Code unequivocally abrogates the sovereign immunity of the United States, states, districts, territories, foreign states, instrumentalities or agencies of any of those governments, and other foreign or domestic governments. That language unambiguously encompasses all governments, including Indian tribes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-227",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16c1f18c99c2c0b3a88a0bf1216fa02155038bf827c4c52533436d86e0f9e5c7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16c1f18c99c2-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
